# CORRIGENDUM to the retained log gen_fu_l31b_nmi_wave_run.log (landing 32, committed a759752).
# The retained log is NOT edited. A retained log is never reopened, so every correction to it lives here, and this
# file carries its own row in gen_manifest.md. It answers CR-31b-L-2 and CM209-Low-2.
#
# WHAT IS WITHDRAWN. The retained log's "THE BUILD" block quotes two figures for the wave build:
#   d71984c246000108   quoted as the compile log's "sources sha256"
#   2bae046d70476d78   quoted as "the root's own filelist_digest"
# Neither is reported by any artefact of that build. Both were typed rather than copied. The error is transcription,
# not a stale build: the retained log's own quoted run header, at its line 19, always carried the true figure, and
# none of the wave readings the log records rests on either withdrawn number.
#
# WHAT EACH SOURCE ACTUALLY REPORTS. Three artefacts of the build print ONE value, 96697a6fee7025b4, under three
# different keys, and the run header the retained log quotes verbatim is one of the three:
#   out8/compile.log line 1154               key "sources sha256:"
#   out8/config_opts.txt line 2              key "sources sha256 (dv/auto_dv env, tb, isa, gen_tb):"
#   out8/irq_nmi_window/run_header.txt       key "build_sources_sha256="
# That value is the LOCAL RUNNER'S find-digest over dv/auto_dv env, tb, isa and gen_tb, written by gen_tb_local.sh.
# It is NOT the committer's gate digest, which is gen_flow_util.filelist_digest over gen_rtl.f plus gen_tb.f. The two
# are different functions over different input sets; the committed tool dv/auto_dv/tools/gen_build_identity.py names
# both keys in its own docstring. So 96697a6fee7025b4 must not be compared against any landing's identity.
#
# THE ROOT'S OWN FILELIST DIGEST IS MEASURED HERE, NOT ONLY WITHDRAWN. The second withdrawn figure was labelled
# filelist_digest, which is a real key with a committed tool that prints it, so the honest correction is the measured
# value rather than a bare withdrawal: the tool reads this root as 32ee156a5dd888e8.
#
# NO GATE IDENTITY OF A COMMITTED BUILD APPLIES TO THIS ROOT. It is an out-of-tree copy carrying the take-trigger
# diff and the uncommitted NMI knob, a shape that was NEVER COMMITTED, so no landing's identity is claimed for it and
# 32ee156a5dd888e8 is that root's own number, for reproduction only.
#
# THE DEBUG FLAGS, CORRECTED. The retained log says the build compiled "-debug_access+all". The compile command, line
# 3 of the compile log, carries BOTH: -debug_access+pp as its third token from the flow's base flags and
# -debug_access+all as its fifth, appended by the scratch copy of gen_tb_local.sh. So the build had FULL debug access
# and this run does not measure whether the cheaper flag alone can dump. config_opts.txt echoes only the base flags,
# which is why it shows +pp alone; treat "can +pp dump" as UNMEASURED. The committed runner compiles +pp and has no
# dump option, which is what made the scratch copy necessary.
#
# WHAT STANDS IN THE RETAINED LOG, unchanged and not re-litigated here: the sweep width 1..8 with the 1..17 and
# 28-firing note (stated in all three of its headers, so no edit is owed); the eleven firings and the first at
# 3655000 ps, cycle 361; the eleven UVM errors; the dump route (-ucli -do against the flow's own gen_dump.tcl
# rendered for gen_tb_top and u_dut, fsdbDumpvars 0 +all plus fsdbDumpSVA on the DUT scope); and the FSDB named by
# path, size and md5 as non-durable scratch.
#
# WHERE ELSE THE WITHDRAWN FIGURES APPEARED. dv/auto_dv/work/tb-infra/STATUS.md carried the same two figures in its
# wave paragraph; they are corrected in the same landing as this file. No other committed file quotes either figure.

